WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
everybody.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.837
I'm so happy to have the studio
audience back.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.772
The energy is great
and honestly --

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.940
-Hey, hey, Seth?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.075
A-Are we allowed to give tickets
to friends again?

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.844
-Very sorry,
that's one of my very rude

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:14.346
writers, Mike Scollins,
everybody.

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:17.683
-Uh --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.852
Yeah,
now that we have audiences back,

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:24.557
a friend wants to come in June.
-You're asking me about June?

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.593
-Yeah, do you know who the
guests are that night?

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:30.930
-Seven months from now?
-I know it's far out,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.298
I just need to make sure
it's not a current

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.401
or former President.
Or Vice President.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:40.439
Or member of Congress. Or other
senior administration official.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.576
-What?
-And just to be safe,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.946
not Jodie Foster.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.748
-Scollins, who did you get
tickets for?

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:53.586
-John Hinckley Jr.
-Are you serious?!

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.188
-Oh, oh it's not the John
Hinckley Jr. you're thinking of.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.691
-Oh, it's not the one who tried
to assassinate Ronald Reagan?

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.861
-Oh, okay no it is the John
Hinckley Jr. you're thinking of.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.664
-Why would you invite him to the
show next year?!

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.500
-Well, he can't come now,
he's committed.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.970
But, he's fully getting out
in June.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.505
-And you think it'd be
appropriate to have

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.008
John Hinckley Jr.
in the audience?

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.109
-Would you rather him as a
guest?

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.246
I don't know how his anecdotes
are gonna be.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.282
Hasn't really done much lately.
-I don't want him here at al--

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.051
How do you even know him?

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.152
-How do you even know
Terry Gross? I don't know.

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:28.721
You just meet people.

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.424
-I'm sorry, Scollins,
but John Hinckley Jr.'s

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.559
not invited here.
-[ Inhales sharply ]

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:36.662
Seth, it's like the judge said,
if he hadn't tried to

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.666
kill the President, he would've
been unconditionally released

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.969
a long, long, long time ago!

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:47.139
-The judge did not say that.
-The judge said exactly that.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:50.310
-Oh, boy.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.445
-You're the one who said
you're excited to have

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.980
an audience back.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:57.817
Is John Hinckley Jr. not "woke"
enough for your liberal agenda?

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.653
[ Laughter ]
-Honestly no.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.489
Wait, actually, what are
John Hinckley's politics?

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.092
-I'm actually not sure.
He's, like, weirdly a-political

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.994
for a presidential assassin.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.062
[ Laughter ]
He weirdly is.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.198
Why is he even being released?

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.934
-Well, his therapist is retiring
in January, so.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.236
-That can't be true.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.639
Wow.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.708
Still, I'm sorry, Scollins, I
don't want your friend,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.510
John Hinckley Jr. in the studio.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.811
-Alright. I'll tell him, but,
heads up,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.280
he doesn't handle
disappointment well.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.515
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.684
-Are you gonna get me killed?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.653
-Guess it depends on how
Jodie Foster feels about you.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.754
-Get outta here!

